{"n": 895, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "895.webp", "text": "5100 ... INFORMATION FOR REPAIRING PLASTIC PARTS:\n\nThe plastic part repairing conditions mentioned below conform with legislation\nIn the Federal Republic of Germany. Always conform with pertinent legislation\nIn e different country.\n\nThese repairing Instructions are provided for qualified workers and assumes\nthelr skill, consclentiousness and sense of responsibility. The Instructions are\nlimited to factory approved repairing methods as well as associated tips and\nmeasures to make the work easler. Only general working procedures are de-\nscribed In these Instructions. The scope of work and order of procedures will\nalways have to be adapted to the pertinent damage condition. Repairs are an\n‘economical solution, so that optical deficiency cannot be excluded. Repairs\nshould therefore only be carried out with explicit customer approval.\n\nThe following E 30 parts are made of plastic and can be repaired with 3M\nRepair Material 5900.\n\n— M-Technique body attachments\n\n= Standard, M3 and Touring rear spollers\n\n— Four wheel drive and M3 entrance and side panels\n\n— Bumpers beginning with 1988 models\n\nimportant!\n\nOnly such damage, which does not have Influence on the strength and rigid-\npepethcbaind apartment eta The following types of damage may not\n— Damage on body mounting points.\n\n= Damage In immediate vicinity of body mounting points.\n\n= Peel-olfs.\n\n— Ruptures.\n\n- Cracks, extending trom comers and edges.\n\n- Continuous cracks with a length of more than 100 mm (4°).\n\n— Holes trom a size of 100 mm* (1.5 In.*) on.\n\nParts with these types of damage must be replaced!\n\nRefer to the BMW Painting Manual for information on painting plastic paris.\n\n51-100\n\nRequired Materials:\n\nAluminous abrasive fiber discs, grain size P 36 and P 80\nSandpaper, grain size P 180\n\n3M Cement Remover 8984\n\n3M Aluminum Adhesive Tape Scotch 424\n\n3M Glass Grid Fabric 9030\n\n3M Plastic Repair Material 5900\n\nMask\n\nGloves\n\nSource of Supply: HWB\n\nretieroeut\n\nSafety Precautions:\n\nExtracting of grinding abrasion.\n\nWearing mask and gloves while grinding.\nWorking only in well ventilated rooms.\nWashing hands frequently.\n\nStoring food separately.\n\nNot eating, drinking or smoking while working.\nNot inhaling vapors.\n\nFirst Ald;\n\nTake off dirty clothes immediately. If dust has gotten in eyes, rinse out with\nwater thoroughly and go to a physician.\n\nHf great amount of vapors are inhaled, go outdoors In fresh air and, If necessary.\nvisit a physician.\n\ninformation on Toxicology:\n\nirritates eyes, skin and the respiratory track. No damaging effects are known as\njong as handling Is corréct.\n\nMeasures in Case of Fire;\nFire extinguishing agents: powders, foam, CO, halon, water mist.\n\nScrapping:\n\nNever let It get Into drink water systems.\n\nSingle components of the repair material must be scrapped as special refuse.\nAtter mixing the single components and hardening, It can be brought to the nor-\nmal refuse station.", "words": [["5100", 0.0318, 0.0923, 0.0625, 0.1042], ["...", 0.0706, 0.1003, 0.0857, 0.1042], ["INFORMATION", 0.0917, 0.0923, 0.1689, 0.1042], ["FOR", 0.1729, 0.0923, 0.1961, 0.1042], ["REPAIRING", 0.2011, 0.0923, 0.2631, 0.1042], ["PLASTIC", 0.2671, 0.0923, 0.315, 0.1042], ["PARTS:", 0.3191, 0.0923, 0.3574, 0.1042], ["The", 0.0318, 0.1253, 0.0534, 0.1372], ["plastic", 0.0549, 0.1227, 0.0917, 0.1438], ["part", 0.0968, 0.1227, 0.1174, 0.1438], ["repairing", 0.12, 0.1266, 0.1678, 0.1412], ["conditions", 0.1709, 0.1266, 0.2288, 0.1372], ["mentioned", 0.2354, 0.1227, 0.2878, 0.1438], ["below", 0.2944, 0.1227, 0.3231, 0.1438], ["conform", 0.3291, 0.1253, 0.373, 0.1372], ["with", 0.377, 0.1253, 0.3992, 0.1372], ["legislation", 0.4032, 0.1253, 0.4582, 0.1398], ["In", 0.0328, 0.1425, 0.0423, 0.153], ["the", 0.0474, 0.1425, 0.0645, 0.1544], ["Federal", 0.0675, 0.1425, 0.1069, 0.1544], ["Republic", 0.1109, 0.1425, 0.1568, 0.157], ["o